  "description": "<p>Given the following sparql-update command:</p>\n\n<p>INSERT </p>\n{\r\n&lt;http://localhost:8080/rest/foo&gt; dc:contributor &lt;http://localhost:8080/rest/foo#contributor&gt; .\r\n&lt;http://localhost:8080/rest/foo#contributor&gt; a foaf:Person ;\r\n\t\tfoaf:name \"me\" .\r\n}\n<p> WHERE {}</p>\n\n<p>The JMS system sends out two messages (this makes sense). But the one referring to the hash container has a strangely formatted IDENTIFIER: in this case it would be /foo/#/contributor, which doesn't seem right. I would expect /foo#contributor</p>",
